kill the non-equivalent mutants of patch 06 that review mutation runs found surviving) by
pinning the paths it rewrites that no other test reaches. Their expected values are computed
from the upstream source at 7caec76 (CLOUD_METADATA_HOSTS, is_disallowed_metadata_hostname,
is_disallowed_metadata_host, is_disallowed_metadata_ipv4/ipv6, is_http_url,
is_loopback_metadata_host, is_allowed_metadata_url, AddressClass::of,
resolve_resource_metadata_url, is_same_origin, validate_authorization_response_issuer,
validate_authorization_metadata_issuer, expected_issuer_for_authorization_metadata_url,
issuer_identifiers_match, validate_resource_metadata_resource, is_resource_identifier_valid),
not from the Lean model. They call only functions with the same name and signature before and
after patch 06: d5_a05_metadata_host_names (A05, patch 06 H1/H2: the three cloud-metadata names
exactly, in mixed case and with trailing dots, `localhost`, `localhost.`, the `.localhost`
suffix in mixed case, and near misses such as notlocalhost, localhost.example,
a.localhost.example (a suffix, not a substring) and metadata.azure; also through
is_allowed_metadata_url), d5_a06_private_ip_targets (A06, H4: an IPv6 and an IPv4 private
literal are allowed exactly with allow_private, loopback literals never, for a non-loopback
base), d5_a07_resolve_trim_empty_unparsable (A07, H5: surrounding ASCII
white space, U+00A0, U+0085 and U+3000 are trimmed, U+FEFF is kept (percent-encoded into the
URL), an all-white-space value gives None, a value that neither parses nor joins gives None),
d5_a07_same_origin (is_same_origin: ASCII case of the host ignored, also for an opaque host of
a non-special scheme; a non-ASCII letter not; default port against explicit default port),
d5_a09_issuer_root_slash (H8: only a root URL may differ by one trailing slash, including a
URL whose query ends in `/`), d5_a08_response_issuer_paths (A08, H6: every path, with the
exact AuthError variant and payload, and an exact, not slash-tolerant, comparison) and
d5_a09_metadata_issuer_paths (A09, H6/H7: with and without allow_missing_issuer, an explicit or
a derived expected issuer (query and fragment dropped, root path, OpenID Connect path-appended
form), none at all, and both mismatch payloads), d5_a09_expected_issuer_forms (H7: the issuer
of each discovery URL form; the path-appended form strips every leading slash, `//t1` and
`///t1` give `/t1`; no issuer for other paths) and d5_a10_resource_identifier_port (A10, H10:
a differing explicit port is a mismatch, the known default port is not; through
validate_resource_metadata_resource with the exact ResourceMismatch payload),
d5_a06_non_http_target (A06, H4: an ftp URL with a public host is never allowed, with or
without allow_private, and resolve_resource_metadata_url rejects it for an http base),
d5_a06_loopback_base_target (A06, H4: a loopback base allows a disallowed target only if the
target is loopback too; 169.254.169.254 and metadata.google.internal are refused, 127.0.0.1 is
