Why (plan Section 19, "Tests (human decision H3)"; Section 21, H3; human decision
2026-11-25): new Rust tests of these functions must live in SDK *.rs files, which stay
byte-identical to upstream. The S34 upstream-test map (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md) found
96 uncovered and 8 partial plan Section 22 cases; this patch covers them. The spec-cycle review
of R09-R15 (findings sR2-a-2, sR2-b-4, sR3-a-3) found the expiry edges of seal_at, its rs1
keyring round trip, and the exact messages and fault order of the keyring constructors pinned by
no Rust test (the upstream test
constructor_invariants_are_enforced matches InvalidKeyring(_) and KeyTooShort { .. } only).
Patch 06 replaces auth.rs expressions by equivalent ones (H1-H10); decision AD5 asks for Rust
tests that would catch a non-equivalent rewrite of the paths no upstream test pins (the inlined
host names, the `.localhost` suffix, the trim, the unparsable value, the exact issuer errors).
The 2026-11-27 extension adds a test for each surviving non-equivalent mutant that review
mutation runs of patch 06 reported: H7's trim_start_slashes stripping one slash only, H2's
ends_with replaced by contains, H4's IPv6 arm returning no address class, H10's port clause
dropped, H7's path-appended branch dropped, A06's http(s) check of the target dropped, A06's
loopback check of the target dropped (the SSRF guard of a loopback base), A07's
Url::parse(value) replaced by base_url.join(value), and A10's scheme clause dropped.
A test-only patch is a process exception (VERIFICATION.md Section 4 defines translation patches
as behaviour-preserving edits that make an item translate); plan Section 21 (H3) asks for it to
be recorded in formal/docs/STATUS.md, "Documents", as a further deviation from VERIFICATION.md.

Effect on the translation: none. Charon does not compile #[cfg(test)] items, and every hunk is
at the end of its file, so no translated item moves (the Source: lines of
formal/translation/ are unchanged); checked by translating the copy with patches 01-03 and
comparing it byte for byte with formal/translation/ (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md). The
AD5 tests too are added at the end of auth.rs, inside mod tests; with all thirteen of them the
check was re-run on 2026-11-27 (scripts/aeneas-translate.sh on a scratch copy of the working
tree with patches 01-06, exit 0): the output is byte-identical to formal/translation/.

Evidence in CI: patched-tests.yml runs cargo test --locked --lib on the copy with all patches
(translated features plus macros, overflow checks and debug assertions on), which runs these
